I now have the complete path. Here is the full trace of `POST /api/owners` in execution order.

## Execution order overview

Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid`) → controller `addOwner` (manual required-field checks, telephone normalization + uniqueness, household uniqueness, email normalization, registrationDate default, customerCode) → mapper `toOwner` → service `saveOwner` (`@Transactional`) → JPA `em.persist`. There is **no** `@PrePersist`/`@EntityListeners`/`@EventListener`/`@InitBinder`/interceptor/filter touching owner creation. The only aspect is a JMX call-timer around repositories. Bean Validation on the `Owner` entity itself is effectively bypassed (see note at end).

---

## 1. The mapped controller method

The route is defined on the generated interface, implemented by the controller.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java` — the interface is `@Validated` (line 44), path constant `PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"` (line 52), and the mapping (lines 79-87):

```java
@RequestMapping(method = RequestMethod.POST, value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,
    produces = { "application/json" }, consumes = { "application/json" })
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true)
    @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
) { ... }
```

So the effective annotations are `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, and `@Validated` on the interface triggers method-parameter validation. Combined with `@RequestMapping("/api")` on the class, the full path is `POST /api/owners`.

The implementing method: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` lines 113-145:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    List<String> missingFields = new ArrayList<>();
    requireNonBlank(missingFields, "firstName", ownerFieldsDto.getFirstName());
    requireNonBlank(missingFields, "lastName", ownerFieldsDto.getLastName());
    requireNonBlank(missingFields, "address", ownerFieldsDto.getAddress());
    requireNonBlank(missingFields, "city", ownerFieldsDto.getCity());
    requireNonBlank(missingFields, "telephone", ownerFieldsDto.getTelephone());
    if (!missingFields.isEmpty()) {
        throw new MissingRequiredFieldsException(missingFields);
    }
    String normalizedTelephone = normalizeTelephone(ownerFieldsDto.getTelephone());
    requireUniqueTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())) {
        requireUniqueHousehold(ownerFieldsDto.getLastName(), ownerFieldsDto.getAddress());
    }
    ownerFieldsDto.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
    if (ownerFieldsDto.getEmail() != null) {
        ownerFieldsDto.setEmail(normalizeEmail(ownerFieldsDto.getEmail()));
    }
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
        owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
    }
    owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getLastName()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Note it operates on `OwnerFieldsDto`, **not** the `Owner` entity. `@PreAuthorize` requires role `OWNER_ADMIN` before any of this runs.

### Controller helper methods (same file)

These run in the order called above.

`requireNonBlank` (258-262) — adds field name to the list if null/blank.

`normalizeTelephone` (275-282) → `toE164` (289-305): strips whitespace/dashes/brackets; if it starts with `+`, keeps the digits; otherwise assumes country code `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; result must match `[0-9]{8,15}` else returns null → `normalizeTelephone` throws `InvalidFieldValueException("telephone", ...)`. Example: `"0412 345 678"` → `"+61412345678"`.

`requireUniqueTelephone` (330-339): loads **all** owners, maps each stored telephone through `toE164`, and throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` if any equals the incoming normalized number.

`requireUniqueHousehold` (351-360) — only called when `sharesHousehold != TRUE`: loads all owners and compares last name + address after `normalizeForHousehold` (367-369: trim, collapse whitespace, lowercase); throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` on match.

`normalizeEmail` (315-321) — only called when email is non-null: trims, validates against `EMAIL_PATTERN = ^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$` (line 68), throws `InvalidFieldValueException("email", ...)` if invalid, else returns lowercased.

`nextCustomerCode` (248-252): `<first 3 letters of lastName uppercased>-<NNNN>` where NNNN = (count of all owners + 1), zero-padded to 4 digits (e.g. `SMI-0007`). This calls `findAllOwners().size()` — a second full-table load.

Side effects in the controller: mutates the incoming DTO (`setTelephone`, `setEmail`), sets `registrationDate` default and `customerCode` on the entity, and issues 3 full `findAllOwners()` scans (uniqueness telephone, uniqueness household, customer code) before saving.

---

## 2. Request DTO and its Bean Validation annotations

